▲ [WARNING] Comparison with NaN using the "==" operator here is always false [equals-nan]

    testdata/logger/src/cli-warn-id.js:1:6:
      1 │ if (a == NaN) b()
        ╵       ~~

  Floating-point equality is defined such that NaN is never equal to anything, so "x === NaN" always returns false. You need to use "Number.isNaN(x)" instead to test for NaN.

